<title>GERMANY: Key German sugar area expects average beet yield.</title>
<headline>Key German sugar area expects average beet yield.</headline>
<dateline>BRAUNSCHWEIG, Germany 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A spokesman for key northern German producer Zuckerverbund Nord AG (ZVN) said beet yields at ZVN this year could be 50 tonnes per hectare.</p>
<p>This would compare with last year's final pan-German figure of 50.7 tonnes per hectare but would be above the 48.4 tonnes recorded last year in Lower Saxony state, where ZVN operates.</p>
<p>He added the figure could change dramatically if the weather changed in the 2-1/2 months left to go until harvesting.</p>
<p>Beet in the ZVN growing regions looked strong and healthy and was aided by warm weather and plenty of rain.</p>
<p>Harvesting is expected to start in mid-September.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
